(a) By July 1, 2026, the commissioner of public safety must amend Minnesota Rules, part 7410.2500, subpart 5, by adding an item F, to no longer require an annual physician's statement from a driver if:





 (1) a single nonepileptic seizure was responsible for the driver's loss of consciousness or voluntary control;





 (2) the driver has been free from episodes of loss of consciousness or voluntary control for five years from the date of the incident under clause (1); 





 (3) the driver has not been prescribed or taking any antiseizure medication for five years from the date of the incident under clause (1); and

Minnesota Statutes 2024, section 124D.094, is amended by adding a subdivision to read:







 Nonresident students.





 (a) Notwithstanding section 126C.05, subdivision 1, or any other law to the contrary, and except as provided under paragraph (c), the average daily membership and pupil units for a student who is not a resident of Minnesota and who is enrolled in online instruction under this section must be counted as though the student were a resident of Minnesota if:





 (1) the student was previously a resident of Minnesota and enrolled in a Minnesota public school in kindergarten through grade 12 up to the age of 21;





 (2) the student is expected to graduate or reestablish residency in Minnesota after no more than 150 calendar days;





 (3) for a student under the age of 18, the student has a parent or guardian who is a resident of Minnesota;

